.TH SHADHIN-BROWSER 1 "November 2026" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shadhin-browser \- Fast, private, and open native Linux web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shadhin-browser
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURL\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBShadhin Browser\fR (স্বাধীন ব্রাউজার) is a native Linux web browser built with
Rust, GTK4, Libadwaita, and WebKitGTK 6.0. It features hardware-accelerated
multi-process rendering, native content filtering, isolated workspaces,
and a glassmorphism theme designed for GNOME and Linux desktops.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of available command-line options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the software version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open a new browser window in the active or a new instance.
.TP
.B \-\-private\-window
Open a new ephemeral private browsing window. No history, cookies, or cache are persisted to disk.
.TP
.BI \-\-new\-tab " URL"
Open the specified URL in a new tab within the current or a new window.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile\-dir " PATH"
Run the browser using an isolated profile directory. The path must be absolute, non-world-writable, and is created with mode 0700.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/shadhin-browser/config.toml
Main user configuration file (permissions 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/shadhin-browser/shadhin.db
SQLite database storing bookmarks, history, shortcuts, and workspaces (permissions 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/shadhin-browser/sessions/
Directory holding per-workspace WebKit network sessions and cookie jars (permissions 0700).
